.\" Manpage for bob (Bodyguard Of Bits)
.\" Format: man-7 (groff_man). Render with: man -l man/bob.1
.\" Contact: cedricclauzel@mailo.com to correct errors or typos.
.TH BOB 1 "2026-10-31" "BOB 0.29.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bob \- Bodyguard Of Bits, a Linux hardening auditor with CIS benchmark mapping
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo bob
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bob
audits a Linux system against a curated set of hardening checks (firewall,
SSH, kernel sysctl, services, file permissions, MAC policy, auditd, …) and
reports findings with severity levels (OK / INFO / WARN / ALERT). It produces
a colourised terminal summary, an optional detailed log file, and an optional
JSON output for scripting.
.PP
.B bob
is audit-only: it never modifies system state without explicit user
confirmation (see
.B \-\-fix
and
.B \-\-apply
below). The
.B \-\-offline
mode disables all outbound network calls and is recommended for distro
build sandboxes and air-gapped environments.
.PP
.B bob
audits only as root (it exits with \(lqThis script must be run as root\(rq
otherwise): run
.BR "sudo bob" ,
or
.B doas
on a host without sudo (with BOB's full path until
.B \-\-install\-completion
has created
.IR /usr/local/bin/bob ). Even as root, a file it cannot read
is reported as not verified, and the score then reads as a ceiling.
The options \fB\-\-help\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR, \fB\-\-explain\fR, \fB\-\-history\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\fR,
\fB\-\-unignore\fR, \fB\-\-test\-email\fR and \fB\-\-test\-webhook\fR need no root.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Audit control
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print, under each finding, its detail, its command, its note and its CIS
reference (an ALERT shows its detail without this flag), plus the raw
listening-port table and the output of
.BR "ufw status verbose" .
.TP
.B \-\-exhaustive
Also run the slow, full-coverage checks that are held out of the default fast
audit: package-file integrity (\fBrpm \-Va\fR / \fBdebsums \-c\fR /
\fBapk audit\fR / \fBpacman \-Qkk\fR), which re-hashes every packaged file and
excludes configuration files, and a sweep of local filesystems for
world-writable files, world-writable directories without the sticky bit and
unowned files (\fBworld_writable\fR; a path other accounts cannot traverse is
reported as latent). Both are INFO-only and never deduct. Opt-in because each
takes tens of seconds to minutes. Naming either section with \fB\-\-check\fR
without this flag reports that it needs it.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-detailed
Write a detailed audit report to the configured log directory
.RI ( ~/.local/share/bob/logs/
by default). Each finding is followed by its explanation, its command
(\(-> for a fix, ? for a check) and its finding key, whatever the terminal
verbosity and under
.B \-\-quiet
too.
.TP
.B \-\-target=\fIN\fR
Set a security score target in 1\(en10. When the resulting score is below
.IR N ,
or when anything could not be read, so the score is not fully verified,
.B bob
exits with code
.B 4
(see
.B EXIT CODES
below). Useful in CI.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-days=\fIN\fR
Analyse UFW logs over the past
.I N
days (default 7). Affects blocked-attempts statistics, top source IPs, and
bruteforce detection windows.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-dir=\fIPATH\fR
Override the detailed report save directory for this run. Does not persist
to
.IR ~/.config/bob/config.conf .
A directory chosen here is not confined to the invoking user's home: run with
sudo, BOB writes the report there and hands it back to that user, as asked.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all terminal output. Use the exit code to detect issues.
Implies neither
.B \-d
nor
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-color ", " \-\-no\-colour
Disable ANSI escape sequences in terminal output.
.B \-\-no\-colour
is an accepted spelling of the same flag.
.
.SS Output formats
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Emit the audit summary to standard output as JSON
.RB ( schema_version
.BR \(dq3\(dq ).
Suppresses the human-readable terminal box. See
.B JSON OUTPUT
below.
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-json\-full
Like
.BR \-\-json ,
but includes per-finding, per-service, per-port detail (large payload).
.TP
.B \-\-html
Long\-form alias of
.BR \-\-format=html .
.TP
.BR \-\-format=\fIFMT\fR ", " \-\-output=\fIFMT\fR
Where
.I FMT
is one of
.BR json ", "
.BR json\-full ", "
.BR csv ", "
.BR markdown ", or "
.BR html .
Text is the default output when no format flag is set;
.B \-\-format=text
is not accepted (rejected at CLI parse time).
.
.SS Configuration and i18n
.TP
.B \-\-lang=\fICODE\fR
Set interface language. Currently supported:
.B en
(default) and
.BR fr .
When neither
.B \-\-lang
nor
.B \-\-french
is given,
.B bob
auto-detects the locale from
.BR LC_ALL ,
.BR LC_MESSAGES ,
or
.B LANG
(POSIX precedence). Falls back to English on
.BR C ,
.BR POSIX ,
or an unsupported locale.
.TP
.B \-\-french
Shorthand for
.BR \-\-lang=fr .
Overrides the locale detection.
.TP
.B \-\-english
Shorthand for
.BR \-\-lang=en .
Overrides the locale detection. Added in v0.12.1 for symmetry with
.BR \-\-french .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reconfigure
Delete the saved configuration
.RI ( ~/.config/bob/config.conf )
and exit. Always asks for confirmation; answering anything but
.B y
leaves the file untouched. Later runs fall back to their defaults: the audit
profile returns to the automatic choice
.RB ( server ,
or
.B desktop
when a display manager is active), and
.B \-\-manage\-logs
asks for a log directory again.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-profile=\fINAME\fR
Apply an audit profile that adjusts severity overrides per finding key.
Built-in profiles:
.BR server " (default), "
.BR desktop ", "
.BR workstation ", "
.BR container .
A valid name is saved as your default for later runs; an invalid one warns,
runs that audit with
.BR server ,
and is not saved. With no profile given or saved,
.B bob
uses
.BR desktop
when
.B display-manager.service
is active, else
.BR server .
User profiles in
.IR ~/.config/bob/profiles/*.conf
take precedence. See
.BR bob-profile (5).
.
.SS Comparison and history
.TP
.B \-D, \-\-diff [\fIPATH\fR]
Show only the delta vs a baseline (new findings, resolved findings, score
change). With no argument, loads the local auto-managed baseline at
.IR ~/.config/bob/last_baseline.json .
With a path argument
.RB ( "\-\-diff " "\fIPATH\fR or " "\-\-diff=" "\fIPATH\fR)" ,
compares against the file at that path \(em useful for
.B cross-machine
or
.B historical
comparison (audit on host A, save the baseline, copy to host B, run
.B sudo bob \-\-diff
.IR /path/to/A-baseline.json
on host B). The path is read-only; the local auto-managed baseline is
untouched.
.IP
The baseline records the source hostname; on cross-machine compare, an
.B INFO
notice surfaces with the recorded vs current hostnames so the operator
knows they are looking at a non-local diff. Pre-v0.9.0 baselines lack
the hostname field and the notice is suppressed.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-baseline
Wipe the comparison baseline file
.RI ( ~/.config/bob/last_baseline.json )
and exit. The next audit run will become the new baseline. Use this after
a major system change to avoid noisy "new findings" lists.
.TP
.B \-\-history
Display a sparkline of the last 50 audit scores from
.IR ~/.config/bob/history.jsonl ,
then a table of the last 10.
.TP
.B \-\-breakdown ", " \-B
Run the audit without its usual terminal output and print the complete score
computation (deductions, caps, per-domain scores). Useful for understanding why the final score is what
it is.
.
.SS Remediation
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fix
Preview the available fixes after the audit (dry run): the commands
.B bob
can apply, the ones it only shows, and the findings that need a manual fix.
Nothing is executed.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Requires
.BR \-\-fix .
Execute the applicable fixes, each after a
.RB \(dq y/N \(dq
prompt. Only commands with no shell operator and no editor are run.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Requires
.BR "\-\-fix \-\-apply" .
Answer
.B y
to every fix prompt and print the commands applied at the end. It does not
answer the confirmation of
.BR \-\-reconfigure .
.TP
.B \-\-explain=\fIKEY\fR
Display a structured explanation for a single finding key. Pass
.B list
as the
.I KEY
to list all available explain keys (230 keys). With no
.IR KEY ,
open the interactive picker.
.TP
.B \-e
Shortcut for
.BR \-\-explain .
.
.SS Network and integrations
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-offline
Disable all outbound network calls (public IP lookup, webhook POST). Required
for distro build sandboxes; recommended for air-gapped environments.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-webhook=\fIURL\fR
POST the audit summary as JSON to
.IR URL
after the audit. Skipped if
.B \-\-offline
is given.
.TP
.B \-\-test\-email
Send a real test message to the first saved notification address, through the
same transport the scheduled audit uses, and exit. The install wizard only ever
established that a
.B sendmail
binary exists, which a Postfix installed and never configured also satisfies
while delivering nothing; this sends and reports what sendmail actually
answered. Exits 0 when sendmail accepted the message \(em accepted is not
delivered, so check the inbox before relying on the cron notifications.
.TP
.B \-\-test\-webhook
POST a minimal smoke payload to the configured webhook and exit, without
running an audit. Honours
.BR \-\-offline ,
which suppresses the POST. Useful for confirming a webhook URL and format
before relying on them.
.TP
.B \-\-webhook-format=\fIFMT\fR
.I FMT
is
.BR auto " (default — Slack/generic detection from the URL), "
.BR generic ", or "
.BR slack .
.
.SS Periodic audits
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-install\-cron
Run an interactive wizard to install a cron job that audits the system on
a schedule and emails the report. The wizard asks for a name, a schedule, a
time, notification addresses, and then the audit's profile, language and
outbound-probe stance \(em pre-selected from the
.BR \-p ,
the language and the
.B \-\-offline
given to this command (without
.BR \-p ,
the saved profile, else
.BR server ).
When no
.B bob
is found on root's PATH, the script calls the one being run, and the wizard
warns if the path it writes does not exist. Those
three are pinned into the generated script because cron runs as root: without
them the scheduled audit would read root's saved profile rather than yours,
and cron's bare environment, where
.B $LANG
is normally unset. The resulting command line is shown before anything is
written. Installed cron jobs are not changed by an upgrade; re-run this wizard
with the same name to regenerate one. On a host without
.I /etc/cron.d
(BusyBox crond on Alpine reads
.IR /etc/crontabs/ )
the wizard refuses before the first question and explains how to use root's
crontab instead.
.TP
.B \-\-manage\-cron
Manage installed cron jobs (list, edit schedule/email, delete).
.TP
.B \-\-watch\fR[\fB=\fIN\fR]
Re-run a silent audit every
.I N
seconds (default 60, minimum 10) until interrupted with Ctrl\-C, printing
each time only what changed since the previous run.
.
.SS Filters
.TP
.B \-\-check=\fIA,B,…\fR
Run only the named sections (prefix matching:
.B kernel
matches
.BR kernel_hardening " and " kernel_modules ).
Core checks
.RB ( firewall ,
.BR firewall_rules ,
.BR ufw_logging ,
.BR firewall_drivers ,
.BR network_context ,
.BR services ,
.BR ports ,
.BR ddns ,
.BR docker ,
.BR virtualization )
always run and cannot be skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-skip=\fIA,B,…\fR
Inverse of
.BR \-\-check .
.TP
.B \-\-min\-level=\fILEVEL\fR
Hide findings below the given severity. Accepted values:
.BR warn " (hide INFO), "
.BR alert " (hide INFO and WARN). "
There is no \fIinfo\fR value (it would be a no-op since INFO is already the floor);
attempting \fB\-\-min\-level=info\fR is rejected at CLI parse time.
Affects the terminal output only; JSON output and the detailed log file
remain complete.
.TP
.B \-\-check=list
Print all available section names (use as the value of \fB\-\-check\fR; there is no separate \fB\-\-list\-checks\fR flag).
.
.SS Misc
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print BOB version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-completion
Install bash completion to
.IR /etc/bash_completion.d/bob
and, when run through
.B sudo
or
.BR doas ,
link
.I /usr/local/bin/bob
to the invoking user's
.IR ~/.local/bin/bob .
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-manage\-logs
Manage stored audit reports (list, view, delete) in the saved report directory
.RI ( ~/.local/share/bob/logs/
by default) and the earlier ones BOB still tracks.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore=\fIKEY\fR
Persistently ignore finding
.I KEY
across all future audits. Stored in
.IR ~/.config/bob/ignore.yml .
.TP
.B \-\-unignore=\fIKEY\fR
Remove
.I KEY
from the ignored-finding list and exit. Mirror of
.B \-\-ignore=KEY \fR;
preserves any operator comments + custom YAML structure in
.IR ~/.config/bob/ignore.yml
(v0.8.1+). Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-ignore .
.TP
.B \-\-show\-ignored
During the audit, display previously-ignored findings as dimmed lines
instead of suppressing them silently. Useful to review what is currently
muted without consulting
.IR ~/.config/bob/ignore.yml
directly. The audit still runs end-to-end \(em this flag does NOT exit
early or dump the ignore file's contents.
.
.SH EXIT CODES
Stable public API. These codes do not change within a major version; new
codes may be added but never removed.
.TP
.B 0
Clean audit \(em no alerts, no warnings.
.TP
.B 1
Warnings detected (improvements suggested).
.TP
.B 2
Alerts detected \(em action required.
.TP
.B 3
Technical error (CLI parsing, IO, internal).
.TP
.B 4
.B \-\-target=\fIN\fR
specified and either the score is below N or anything could not be read: a score nothing
verified cannot satisfy a gate, so it fails closed. Widened in v0.16.2 from
\(lqis an upper bound\(rq, which stops being true when blindness removes a
whole scoring domain.
.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
.B \-\-json
emits a stable JSON contract
.RB ( schema_version
.BR \(dq3\(dq ).
Always-present top-level keys:
.IR schema_version ,
.IR version ,
.IR host ,
.IR timestamp_utc ,
.IR score ,
.IR score_max ,
.IR score_is_upper_bound ,
.IR score_low ,
.IR score_high ,
.IR unscored_domains ,
.IR unverified ,
.IR target ,
.IR target_met ,
.IR risk ,
.IR network_context ,
.IR public_ip ,
.IR alert_count ,
.IR warning_count ,
.IR info_count ,
.IR degraded_sections ,
.IR profile ,
.IR duration_seconds ,
.IR deductions ,
.IR posture_escalation ,
.IR domain_scores .
Full mode
.RB ( \-\-json\-full )
adds
.IR findings ,
.IR services ,
.IR open_ports ,
.IR open_ports_all ,
.IR deductions_raw ,
.IR firewall_drivers ,
and
.IR hardening " and " ipv6
when those sections ran.
.PP
Each deduction and finding carries a stable dotted
.B key
(e.g.
.BR firewall.logging_off )
and an optional
.B template_vars
dict for locale-independent reconstruction of the message via
.B bob.formatter.format_finding .
.PP
See
.IR DOCUMENTS/README_TECH.md " section " "JSON output schema"
for the complete reference.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/config.conf
User configuration (audit profile, webhook, log directory, SUID whitelist). Mode 0600.
See
.BR bob.conf (5).
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/profiles/*.conf
User audit profiles (severity overrides per finding key). See
.BR bob-profile (5).
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/services.d/*.json
User service plugin definitions. JSON Schema:
.IR bob/data/schemas/service.schema.json .
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/checks.d/*.py
Custom Python audit plugins, executed through BOB's in-process sandbox
(SandboxRunner, since v0.7.0). It is defence-in-depth, not a security
boundary: run only plugins you have reviewed.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/last_baseline.json
Snapshot of the previous audit for
.B \-\-diff
comparisons.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/history.jsonl
Append-only score history (rotated at 1000 entries).
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/ignore.yml
Persistently ignored finding keys.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/recurrence.json
Consecutive-audit counter of each ALERT/WARN key.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/emails
Address book of the cron notifications.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bob/logs/
Default detailed-report destination
.RB ( \-d
flag).
.TP
.I /etc/cron.d/bob-NAME
System cron entries installed via
.BR \-\-install\-cron .
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/bob-NAME
The script each cron entry runs.
.TP
.IR /usr/local/bin/bob ", " /etc/bash_completion.d/bob
The sudo-PATH link and the completion script written by
.BR \-\-install\-completion .
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR SUDO_USER ", " DOAS_USER
Honored by BOB to resolve
.RB \(dq ~/.config/bob/ \(dq
to the invoking user's home rather than
.IR /root/
when run via
.B sudo
or (since 0.25.1)
.BR doas ;
.B SUDO_USER
wins when both are set.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
Used for locale auto-detection (POSIX precedence). See
.BR \-\-lang
above.
.TP
.B BOB_SHARE
Absolute path to a share directory (containing
.IR locales/ ", " data/ )
that replaces the data files bundled inside the Python package. Nothing in
BOB's own packaging sets it; when it is unset, or does not resolve to an
absolute directory, the bundled files are used.
.TP
.BR NO_COLOR ", " FORCE_COLOR
Any non-empty value turns colour off, or on even when the output is not a
terminal. Without either, colour follows whether the output is a terminal;
.B \-\-no\-color
wins over both.
.TP
.B BOB_DEBUG
Any non-empty value installs a logging handler (for example, why a service
plugin entry was skipped) and prints the full traceback of a fatal error.
.TP
.B BOB_WEBHOOK_ALLOW_INSECURE
Set to
.B 1
to allow an
.B http://
webhook URL; by default only
.B https://
is accepted.
.
.SH SECURITY
BOB is an audit-only tool that runs with root privileges. It is part of the
.B post-compromise
audit toolchain: a rooted attacker can already lie to BOB about every value
it reads from
.IR /proc/ ", " /sys/ ", " /etc/ .
BOB does not replace a file-integrity scanner (AIDE, Tripwire), an antivirus
(ClamAV), nor a rootkit detector (rkhunter).
.PP
See the project's
.B SECURITY.md
file for the complete threat model and the vulnerability disclosure process.
.
